cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TDDO: a truck-drone joint delivery optimizer"
abstract: >-
  An optimization project for truck-drone tandem delivery with synchronized
  rendezvous, bidirectional loads and time-dependent circular no-fly zones.
  The model is a 79-constraint MILP solved at realistic scale by a custom ALNS,
  with Gurobi used to certify small instances. The project contributes a
  corrected rendezvous formulation (splitting the single recover-or-launch flag
  into separate arrival and departure variables, which lowers the proven optimum
  on 4/4 small instances) and a boundary analysis of the resulting cost
  reduction across hover-energy pricing, swap duration, battery stock, instance
  form and spatial layout.
authors:
